73
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:04,108
And for 0 compared to 1, it would give you

74
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:08,108
back a 0 because you have at least one 0 in

75
00:03:08,156 --> 00:03:08,316
there.

76
00:03:09,425 --> 00:03:11,626
For 1 compared to 0, you therefore also get

77
00:03:11,626 --> 00:03:15,562
0, and for 0 to 0, you also get that. So the

78
00:03:15,626 --> 00:03:18,325
bitwise AND would produce this new binary

79
00:03:18,582 --> 00:03:21,169
number. Now it does that binary stuff behind

80
00:03:21,169 --> 00:03:23,386
the scenes. You use it with decimal numbers,

81
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:25,828
but you get back a 0 because of that

82
00:03:25,828 --> 00:03:27,933
behind-the-scenes work it does, which I just

